## Runbook

### Deploy
```bash
# 1. Clone with submodules
git clone --recurse-submodules <repo-url> && cd agents-arwaky

# 2. Verify prerequisites
./aa doctor

# 3. Full install (submodules → build → launchers → MCP config)
./aa install

# 4. Verify
aa status && aa check

# 5. Connect harnesses
aa connect --all

# 6. Start daemons
aa service start all
```

### Rollback
```bash
# 1. Stop daemons
aa service stop all

# 2. Uninstall all tools
aa uninstall --all

# 3. Reset submodules
git submodule foreach --recursive 'git clean -fd && git checkout .'

# 4. Clean generated artifacts
aa clean --all

# 5. Re-install from known-good commit
git checkout <known-good-tag>
./aa install
```

### Monitor
```bash
# Daemon health
aa anytype status
aa 9router status
aa service status

# Daemon logs
aa anytype logs
aa 9router logs

# Tool readiness
aa status

# Full diagnostics
aa doctor
```

### Incident Response
| Symptom | Diagnosis | Action |
|---------|-----------|--------|
| `aa run <tool>` fails with "not installed" | `aa status` shows tool as Not Installed | `aa install <tool>` |
| Anytype API not ready | `aa anytype status` shows API: not ready | `aa anytype logs` → check for port conflict or missing binary |
| 9Router dashboard unreachable | `aa 9router status` | Check `NINEROUTER_PORT` env, verify Podman is running |
| Harness MCP not loading | `aa connect --all --dry-run` | Verify `mcp_servers.generated.json` is valid JSON, re-run `aa mcp generate` |
| Backup restore fails | Check archive integrity | `tar -tzf <archive>` to verify before restore |
| Skill not found after install | `aa skill check` | `aa skill install all --force` |

